implementationPlan.description:
MINIMUM IMPLEMENTATION. Report every file.

1. moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/services/MoeStateListener.kt:
   - add a top-level `data class DaemonError(val operation: String?, val codeName: String?, val taskId: String?, val message: String)`;
   - add the interface default `fun onDaemonError(error: DaemonError) {}`. Its KDoc says it is delivered AFTER onError for every ERROR frame, and that each field is null when the frame lacks it or carries a non-string;
   - leave the four existing onError implementers untouched.
2. moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/services/MoeMessageDispatcher.kt, "ERROR" branch:
   - keep `publishError(operation, errorMessage)` exactly;
   - then publish `DaemonError(json.get("operation").stringOrNull(), json.get("codeName").stringOrNull(), json.get("context")?.takeIf { it.isJsonObject }?.asJsonObject?.get("taskId").stringOrNull(), errorMessage)` through a new `publishDaemonError`. It runs invokeLater and listeners.forEach { it.onDaemonError(it) }, like publishError;
   - add the private strict accessor `JsonElement?.stringOrNull()`. It returns non-null only for a JSON primitive string and never calls asString on an object or array.
   Error handling: the strict parse cannot throw, so a hostile frame can never suppress the legacy onError delivery.
3. moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/PlanReviewApprovalState.kt: replace `onDaemonError(operation: String, message: String)` with `fun onDaemonError(operation: String?, errorTaskId: String?, codeName: String?): Boolean`, under the existing lock:
   - return false unless operation == APPROVE_OPERATION ("APPROVE_TASK"), errorTaskId == taskId and the phase is PENDING;
   - if codeName == PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH ("PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH", exact), set phase = INVALIDATED and notice = PLAN_CHANGED_KEY, and return true. The approval stays latched, and capturedRevision is never replaced;
   - otherwise call releasePending(DAEMON_ERROR_KEY).
   Add the two constants to the companion object. The KDoc names VS Code PlanReviewPanel.handleClientError as the parity reference.
4. moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/PlanReviewDialog.kt:
   - delete the onError override, so the interface default no-op applies;
   - add `override fun onDaemonError(error: DaemonError) { if (!approval.onDaemonError(error.operation, error.taskId, error.codeName)) return; lastErrorMessage = error.message.take(MAX_ERROR_CHARS); ... }`, followed by the same EDT repaint as before (SwingUtilities.invokeLater with an isDisposed guard and try/log);
   - keep CQ-I06a's onStatus untouched.
Run the focused classes from step 1: all green.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
JetBrains reads codeName and context.taskId from daemon ERROR frames strictly. Only APPROVE_TASK errors for its own task reach the plan-review machine:
- a correlated PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH latches as plan changed;
- any other correlated error re-arms;
- uncorrelated frames never touch a pending approval, so a later WORKING at the captured revision still confirms it.
This matches VS Code's PlanReviewPanel.handleClientError.

acceptanceCriteria:
Machine tests D1-D6 prove:
- correlation by operation, task id and context;
- the exact-match mismatch latch;
- the re-arm for other codes;
- nothing changes outside PENDING.
